  "cameraExplanationTitle": "Camera assistance",
  "cameraExplanationBody": "Posture Guard can use your front camera to help improve posture detection while the app is open.\n\nCamera images are processed on your device, are not saved, and are not uploaded.\n\nCamera access is optional. If you choose not to allow it, posture monitoring will continue using your phone's motion sensors.",
  "notNow": "Not now",
  "cameraActiveIndicator": "Front camera active • Images are not saved",
  "cameraAndPrivacy": "Privacy & PDPA",
  "privacyInformationBody": "The front camera may be used only as an optional posture signal while this app is visible and posture monitoring needs extra help. Images are processed on this device, discarded after analysis, and are never saved or uploaded. You can always use sensor-only monitoring.",
  "privacyPageIntroduction": "Posture Guard is designed to monitor posture while giving you control over how your device data and camera are used.\n\nThe app primarily uses your phone's motion sensors to estimate posture. You may also choose to enable the front camera to help improve posture detection while the app is open.",
  "privacyPageCameraUseTitle": "Camera use",
  "privacyPageCameraUseIntroduction": "The front camera is optional.\n\nIf camera assistance is enabled:",
  "privacyPageCameraUseItems": "The front camera is used only to help estimate your posture.\nCamera images are processed directly on your device.\nCamera images are not saved.\nCamera images are not uploaded to Firebase or any external server.\nCamera images are discarded after processing.\nCamera assistance is used only while the app is active and the feature is needed.",
  "privacyPageCameraUseClosing": "You can turn camera assistance off at any time. Posture Guard will continue monitoring posture using your phone's motion sensors.",
  "privacyPageCameraPermissionTitle": "Camera permission",
  "privacyPageCameraPermissionBody": "Posture Guard will explain why camera access is needed before Android asks for camera permission.\n\nCamera access is optional.\n\nIf you deny camera permission, posture monitoring will continue using motion sensors.\n\nYou can also revoke camera permission later through your device settings.",
  "privacyPageDataStoredTitle": "Data we store",
  "privacyPageDataStoredIntroduction": "Posture Guard may store information needed for the app to work, including:",
  "privacyPageDataStoredItems": "App settings\nPosture calibration\nPosture statistics\nMonitoring history\nCoins\nOwned and equipped cosmetics\nApp progress\nCamera-assistance preferences",
  "privacyPageDataStoredClosing": "Cloud data is stored under your anonymous Firebase account so that your data is separated from other users.\n\nPosture Guard does not require your name, email address, or password to create this anonymous account.",
  "privacyPageFirebaseTitle": "Firebase and cloud data",
  "privacyPageFirebaseBody": "Posture Guard uses Firebase to store and synchronize selected app data.\n\nEach installation is assigned an anonymous Firebase user ID.\n\nYour Firebase user ID is used to keep your cloud data separate from other users.\n\nPosture Guard does not use this anonymous account to identify you by name.",
  "privacyPageChoicesTitle": "Your choices",
  "privacyPageChoicesItems": "Use Posture Guard without the camera.\nTurn camera assistance on or off.\nDeny or revoke camera permission.\nContinue using sensor-based posture monitoring if camera access is unavailable.\nReview this privacy information at any time.\nDelete your Posture Guard data from Settings.",
  "privacyPageDeleteTitle": "Delete your data",
  "privacyPageDeleteBody": "You can use \"Delete my data\" in Settings to remove your Posture Guard cloud data and anonymous Firebase account.\n\nThe app will ask you to confirm before deletion.\n\nIf deletion cannot be completed, Posture Guard will not falsely report that your data has been deleted.",
  "privacyPageCameraIndicatorTitle": "Camera indicator",
  "privacyPageCameraIndicatorBody": "Whenever the front camera is actually active for posture assistance, Posture Guard displays an in-app camera activity indicator.\n\nThis lets you know when the camera is being used.",
  "privacyPageConsentTitle": "Consent and control",
  "privacyPageConsentBody": "Camera assistance is optional and requires your permission.\n\nChoosing not to use the camera does not prevent you from using Posture Guard's main sensor-based posture monitoring.\n\nYou can change your choice at any time in Settings.",
  "privacyPagePolicyTitle": "Privacy policy",
  "privacyPagePolicyBody": "This in-app page provides a summary of Posture Guard's privacy practices.\n\nA hosted Privacy Policy URL will also be provided for the Google Play Store before public release.",
